# Both accounts belong to one maintainer. Listing both is not a claim that two
# people review this code. The intent is that GitHub requests a review from the
# account that did not author the commits, as the prompt to write the objection
# `CONTRIBUTING.md` requires.
#
# Not yet observed on a pull request: CODEOWNERS is read from the base branch,
# so this file cannot take effect until it is on `develop`. Confirm it on the
# first pull request after that and correct this comment if it does not.
#
# That request can only ever be answered with comments. `no-self-approval.yml`
# is a required check on `develop` and fails when either account submits an
# approving review, so an approval here blocks the merge rather than enabling
# it. `develop` requires zero approving reviews, because there is nobody to
# give one.
#
# Code-owner review is deliberately NOT required in branch protection
# (`require_code_owner_reviews: false`, read 2026-09-20). Requiring it would
# create a gate that only an approval can open and that CI refuses to let
# either account open.
#
# That setting lives in the GitHub interface and nothing in this repository
# reads it back, so it is a dated observation like the table in
# CONTRIBUTING.md. See #165.
#
# One rule, because both accounts own everything and per-path lines listing the
# same two owners say nothing the first line has not already said.

